abstract: >-
  Honeypots aid cyber defense but traditional designs demand heavy manual
  setup and support few protocols. We introduce OHRA, a modular, extensible
  LLM-driven honeypot that supports multiple protocols (SSH, Telnet, HTTP,
  FTP, SMTP, SNMP, IPP) and can integrate different LLM providers. OHRA
  wraps the model with session memory and prompt control to generate
  realistic, context-aware responses with less configuration effort. We
  evaluate OHRA against Cowrie and a recent LLM-based honeypot using
  curated malware commands and a real-world Internet deployment. OHRA is
  among the first honeypots to demonstrate a unified LLM-based architecture
  across several protocols: SSH, Telnet, and HTTP are fully interactive,
  while FTP, SMTP, IPP, and SNMP are currently implemented in partial form.
  Results show higher response realism, improved session handling, and
  greater deceptiveness in comparison to prior systems. This work lays the
  groundwork for scalable and adaptive multi-protocol deception platforms.

